POST-RACE UPDATE WORKFLOW (2026 SEASON)
========================================================================

## STEP 1: UPDATE DATA (AUTOMATED)

### For Formula 1:

Run the F1 api_update.py script to automatically fetch and update all F1 data:

    cd src/config/f1
    py api_update.py
    cd ../../../

### For Formula 2:

Change line 8 to the race results page URL in api_update.py
Run the F2 api_update.py script from the root directory (you can paste the results URL if needed):

    py src/config/f2/api_update.py

### For F1 Academy:

Change line 8 to the race results page URL in api_update.py
Run the F1A api_update.py script from the root directory (you can paste the results URL if needed):

    py src/config/f1a/api_update.py

\*Note: The F1 script includes automated data cleaners (like the Kimi Antonelli and Jak Crawford fixes). A full run may take a few minutes depending on rate limits.

## STEP 2: BUILD & PUSH TO GITHUB

1. Generate a new build (this ensures your build folder is perfectly synced):
   npm run build

2. Commit and push ALL changes directly to the main F1-Telemetry repository:
   git add .
   git commit -m "Update race data"
   git push

_Note: You no longer need to run any export scripts or manually upload files to external repositories like f1-telemetry-api, f1aapi, or f2api! The architecture is now 100% self-contained._

## STEP 3: CLEAR LIVE CACHE

By default, your live server caches API data for 30 minutes. If you want your new GitHub pushes to appear instantly, you must clear the cache.

**Option A: The "Nuclear" Option (Recommended for full updates)**
Log into your web hosting panel (IONOS/cPanel) and simply delete the `api_cache/` folder entirely. This forces the server to re-download all files from GitHub on the next page load.

**Option B: Single-File Force Refresh**
If you only need to quickly flush a specific file, visit its API URL with the `?flush=1` parameter appended:

- F1 Standings: https://f1-telemetry.matthews-world.co.uk/api.php?source=f1&path=races/2026/driverStandings.json&flush=1
- F2 Results: https://f1-telemetry.matthews-world.co.uk/api.php?source=f2&path=races/2026/results.json&flush=1
- F1A Results: https://f1-telemetry.matthews-world.co.uk/api.php?source=f1a&path=races/2026/results.json&flush=1
